];
const evidence=[['front','Front panel','Rev C, p. 15: three 4-by-2 groups of BNCs and a left-hand power/trigger cluster. Labels and positions are original approximations.','15'],['rear','Rear panel','Rev C, p. 19: four telegraph inputs, USB-B, DB25 and AC inlet. Option label identifies the selected zero-ANC model.','19'],['oblique','Enclosure and bench host','Rev C, cover: navy enclosure, silver front and rack handles beside a computer. Host and patch lead are illustrative.','1']];
---
<Layout pageTitle="Digidata 1550B · acquisition bench" description="Digitize a calibrated ramp or an amplifier waveform on a metric eight-channel Axon Digidata 1550B model.">
<article class="equipment dd">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/10-02/">← Equipment 10-02</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#dd-ref">References</a><a href="#dd-tests">Verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">10-02 · ELECTROPHYSIOLOGY / DATA ACQUISITION</span><h2>Axon Digidata 1550B</h2><p>Patch a voltage source into a channel, select the acquisition clock, and inspect what survives digitization. This is the base Molecular Devices 1550B without a HumSilencer module, not the earlier 1550/1550A or the ANC options.</p></header>
<div class="dd-grid">
<section><span class="eq-meta">01 / INSPECT</span><h3>Instrument</h3><div id="dd-stage" aria-label="Orbitable Digidata rack with selectable analog input connectors"></div>
<div class="bar" aria-label="Camera views">{['Overall','Front','Inputs','Rear','Station'].map(name=><button data-dd-view={name}>{name}</button>)}
<button id="dd-vr" hidden>Enter VR</button></div><p id="dd-view-status" role="status">Loading instrument…</p>
<p class="hint">Drag to orbit, pinch or scroll to zoom. Select an input BNC in the 3D view to route the signal there. The same action can be performed under Acquisition. A host and cable are shown in Station view.</p></section>
<section><span class="eq-meta">02 / OPERATE</span><h3>Acquisition</h3>
<div class="config"><label>Voltage source<select id="dd-source"><option value="ramp">Calibration ramp · −12 to +12 V</option><option value="clamp">10-01 · MultiClamp primary BNC</option><option value="file">Imported voltage trace</option></select></label>
<label>Import waveform JSON<input type="file" id="dd-file" accept=".json,application/json"/></label>
<label>First analog input<select id="dd-map">{Array.from({length:8},(_,i)=><option value={i}>AI{i}</option>)}</select></label>
<label>Sample rate (Hz)<input id="dd-rate" type="number" value="1000" step="any" min="1" max="500000"/></label></div>
<p id="dd-input-note" class="hint"></p>
<div class="bar"><button id="dd-power">Power on</button><button id="dd-usb">USB connected</button><button id="dd-lead">Source connected</button></div>
<button id="dd-run" class="primary">Acquire record</button><p aria-live="polite" id="dd-status">Loading calibration example…</p>
</section></div>
<section><span class="eq-meta">03 / MEASURE</span><h3>Digitized voltage</h3><div class="results"><div><canvas id="dd-plot" width="900" height="280" aria-label="Digitized voltage versus time; clipping marked at either rail"></canvas><p id="dd-metrics" aria-live="polite">Run an acquisition to see values.</p></div><div class="read"><h4>Probe one sample</h4><label>Input channel<select id="dd-ch" disabled></select></label><label>Sample index<input id="dd-i" type="range" min="0" max="0" value="0" disabled/></label><output id="dd-probe">No record.</output></div></div>
<div class="bar"><button id="dd-json" disabled>Export revision (JSON)</button><button id="dd-csv" disabled>Export samples (CSV)</button><button id="dd-replay" disabled>Export selected channel for scope replay</button></div></section>
<section><h3>How conversion works</h3><p>Use the included calibration ramp or the simulated primary-output volts from the <a href="/simulations/equipment/10-01/">MultiClamp 700B record</a>. The latter is an actual export from the model-cell simulator, not an intracellular voltage in disguise. In this acquisition experiment the source, not the ADC, supplies the waveform. The supplied ramp deliberately exceeds both ADC rails; the imported amplifier run should remain inside them.</p>
<p>At sample n the clock reads <code>t₀ + n/fₛ</code>. Source samples are linearly interpolated onto that clock, up to and including the last available source time. All routed channels are sampled simultaneously. For nominal step <code>q = 20 / 65536 V</code>, signed simulated code <code>k = clamp(round(V/q), −32768, 32767)</code>; reported input voltage is <code>kq</code>. Positive half-step ties round toward positive infinity. Inputs strictly outside ±10 V set a signed overload flag. Exactly +10 V is on range, but reconstructs one step below the positive endpoint. Signed coding and rounding are explicit educational conventions, not a claim about Axon file encoding.</p>
<p><b>Limits.</b> The example is an ideal ADC, not a calibrated physical unit. No anti-alias, front-end bandwidth, jitter, noise, ANC, output waveform generation or ABF serialization. Undersampling can alias. Upsampling a saved trace interpolates it and cannot create new measured information. Physical analog and digital output connectors and rear telegraphs are represented for orientation only.</p>
<details><summary>Input, output and handoff contract</summary><p>Input: <code>bts.analog-waveform.v1</code> with sampleId, revision, dtS in seconds, optional t0S and 1–8 equal-length channels with unique IDs and unit V. Provide at least two input samples per channel; the teaching cap is 250,000 total values per input or output. Values route consecutively from the first selected input; maps beyond AI7 are rejected. Output increments revision, retains IDs and parent provenance, appends AI terminal, signed integer codes, input-referred voltages, overload flags and timing. CSV is a flat view; JSON is the complete provenance-preserving handoff. A separate scope replay CSV includes sample ID, channel ID, revision and source comments. Incompatible clocks, disconnected sources/USB and oversized captures cannot produce an export.</p>
<p><a href={base+'multiclamp-input.json'}>Upstream example</a> · <a href={base+'example-output.json'}>Acquired revision</a> · <a href={base+'output-schema.json'}>Output schema</a></p><p><b>Downstream replay:</b> export the selected channel for the <a href="/simulations/equipment/09-04/">09-04 oscilloscope</a>. This is file replay, not an electrical output. For the supplied <a href={base+'scope-replay.csv'}>MultiClamp → Digidata trace</a>, the MSO64B solver returned 61 samples at 2 kS/s; 45 mV rising trigger at source time 14.5 ms; 74.14 mV peak-to-peak; no clipped points. Settings: 3 ms/div, 20 mV/div, 50 mV vertical center, DC coupling and 10× readout.</p></details></section>
<section id="dd-ref"><span class="eq-meta">04 / EVIDENCE</span><h3>Reference views and scale</h3><p>Original renders from this model, not manufacturer photographs. Compare each with the linked hardware view in <a href={guide}>Molecular Devices user guide 5040237 C (April 2024)</a>. The cabinet envelope is specified; detail positions, mechanical outlines, cable lengths and host are inferred. No factory CAD or internal circuitry is asserted.</p>
<div class="figs">{evidence.map(([file,title,caption,page])=><figure><img src={base+file+'.webp'} alt={'Original Digidata rendering: '+title} loading="lazy"/><figcaption><strong>{title}.</strong> {caption} <a href={guide+'#page='+page}>Compare to source</a></figcaption></figure>)}</div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th><th>How it is used</th><th>Guide page</th></tr></thead><tbody>{spec.map(([a,b,c,d])=><tr><td>{a}</td><td>{b}</td><td>{c}</td><td><a href={guide+'#page='+d}>{d}</a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p><a href={maker}>Manufacturer product and technical resources</a></p></section>
<section id="dd-tests"><span class="eq-meta">05 / VERIFICATION</span><h3>Independent checks</h3><p>Tests below are calculated against analytical references and the selected hardware specification, not a bench-measured performance claim.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Result</th><th>Tolerance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>−12 to +12 V ramp at 1 kHz</td><td>13 samples, 2 overloads; monotone</td><td>13, 2, monotone</td><td>0 counts</td></tr>
<tr><td>±5 V codes</td><td>−16384 / +16384</td><td>−16384 / +16384</td><td>0 counts</td></tr>
<tr><td>2 kHz acquisition of 4 ms ramp</td><td>9 samples, 0.5 ms interval</td><td>9; 0.5 ms</td><td>1 ps</td></tr>
<tr><td>Two inputs mapped to AI6–7</td><td>Shared time; no skew</td><td>Identical clock</td><td>0 sample delay</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active MultiClamp sample</td><td>131 points, no overload; ≤½ LSB interior residual</td><td>131 points, no overload; peak 151.37 µV</td><td>152.59 µV</td></tr>
<tr><td>Unplugged host / invalid rate</td><td>Reject; no stale export</td><td>Rejected</td><td>Exact</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bare hardware bounds W/H/D</td><td>483 / 109 / 363 mm</td><td>483 / 109 / 363 mm</td><td>1 mm</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><p><a href={base+'reference-cases.json'}>Predefined fixtures</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification results</a> · <a href={base+'digidata-1550b.glb'} download>Download metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'build-model.py'} download>Editable parametric model</a> · <a href={base+'adc.mjs'}>Solver and action interface</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR anchors and complexity</a></p>
<p class="hint">VR preparation: glTF meters, bench origin at the cabinet floor, +Y up, +Z operator-facing, named control bounds. A compatible immersive browser can request seated/standing local-floor mode. Physical Quest performance, reach and comfort remain unverified.</p>
</section></article></Layout>
